<BaseLayout title="JuggleCast Community versus Pro" description="Understand JuggleCast Community’s autonomous broadcast path and the boundary around optional, separately licensed Pro capabilities."><section class="page container"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">EDITIONS</p><h1>Community versus Pro</h1><p>The Community broadcast foundation is autonomous. Pro is an optional, separately licensed extension—not a requirement for broadcasting.</p></header><div class="split"><article class="panel"><h2>Community</h2><ul><li>Authenticated station control</li><li>Media, playlists and scheduled programming</li><li>BPM-aware selection and configurable transitions</li><li>Audio analysis, Rust playout and Icecast delivery</li><li>History, diagnostics, backup, restore, updates and rollback</li><li>Best-effort community support without an SLA</li></ul><p><strong>No paid licence or mandatory remote licence-service request is required to start and broadcast.</strong></p></article><article class="panel"><h2>Optional Pro</h2><p>Pro uses a separate commercial licence. Repository documentation identifies Bliss-driven acoustic similarity, music-aware sequence optimisation and advanced transition/programming strategies as optional capabilities.</p><p>Other functions are included only when separately defined and documented. This site makes no roadmap promise.</p></article></div><section class="prose"><h2>Operational boundary</h2><p>If an operator explicitly configures Pro, a licence request may transmit a licence identifier, JuggleCast version, installation identifier, requested entitlement and coarse platform metadata. It does not transmit media, playlists, Icecast secrets or listener data.</p><p>A Pro licensing-service outage must not interrupt Community operation. Service images are separately licensed; the repository’s MIT licence must not be read as a claim that those OCI images’ source is open.</p></section></section><CallToAction/></BaseLayout>
